rust/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Turborepo
.turbo/

# Log files
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

.graphifyignore
graphify-out

# Research paper LaTeX/PDF build output (`pnpm gen:papers`)
docs/research/build/

# Generated agent corpus (regenerated by gen-llms.mjs during build; not tracked to avoid churn)
apps/site/public/llms.txt
apps/site/public/llms-full.txt

# CLAUDE.md is the project agent guide — track it here despite any global ignore
!CLAUDE.md

# observatory: the bundle is a generated capture, re-emitted from the runtime
apps/observatory/public/bundle.json

# Root-level agent files stay local tooling config. The shared, tool-agnostic agent knowledge base
# lives in .agents/ and IS tracked — re-included explicitly, because many global gitignores (and
# .git/info/exclude files) ignore `.agents/` and `AGENTS.md` everywhere; repo rules take precedence.
# Only its generated corpus (tools/gen-llms.py → .agents/llms*.txt) stays ignored.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
!.agents/
!.agents/**
.agents/llms*.txt
.agents/**/.DS_Store
apps/llms-full-fe.txt

# RC-7 gate output on the runner (scripts/perf, perf-hardware.yml); committed measurements live in docs/planning/perf-measurements/
/perf/

